34,2,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"The bay holds only four hundred kilos. Plus, six evenings are already booked for events. The room is already full.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The data is clear. People return for presence and movement, not static cases. We must prioritize exhibits that offer interaction or change.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, interaction is great, but the lab is drowning! Two hundred pieces are stuck, and only one person is working. We can’t even clean the objects!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, that’s bad, but my paperwork check shows two recent openings slipped past shipping cut-offs. We can’t even get the boxes here on time!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, timing is vital, but my numbers show transport and mounting eat a third of the budget. We need self-supporting pieces to stop the bleeding.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Benjamin, self-supporting pieces are good, but the floor limit is strict. We must avoid heavy items entirely to keep the structure safe.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, the weight limit is a hard constraint. We need light, dynamic displays. Presence without mass.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Daisuke, light is good, but who moves it? The volunteers are just history walkers! We need real staff, not just names on a list!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, I found seventeen breakdowns last season! If the powered displays fail, the room is empty. We need reliable tech, not just more people.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, reliability is key, but every powered unit adds to the maintenance backlog. We need exhibits that don’t require constant, expensive intervention.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I’m worried. If the floor is weak and the room is busy, adding heavy or complex items feels too risky.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, risk is manageable. The data proves static displays fail. We need light, dynamic presence to ensure return visits.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, dynamic is great, but who actually runs it? The lab is empty! We need a plan for real people, not just fancy lights!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, I agree, but my logs show powered displays broke down seventeen times! If the tech fails, the room is empty. We need reliable, simple items.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, I agree. Simplicity saves money. If we avoid powered units, we dodge the maintenance trap and keep the budget intact.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I’m sorry, I’m still anxious. The floor limit and the evening events make me feel we shouldn’t add anything heavy or complex.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, I hear your caution. But the data is undeniable. We need light, dynamic presence. Let’s find a candidate that fits these strict limits.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, I hear you, but without staff, ""dynamic"" is just a disaster waiting to happen! We need a plan for real people, not just fancy lights!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, I hear you. But if the tech breaks, it’s a disaster anyway. Let’s pick something simple and sturdy that won’t fail us.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, I hear you. But simplicity is the only budget that survives. Let’s pick something sturdy that doesn’t need a mechanic or a miracle.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
