61,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, Option A fits. Light textiles, live presence, no heavy rigging. It satisfies the data and your structural limits.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, wait! Option C has a working conservation bench! That means real staff are actually doing the work, not just volunteers!","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, I worry about the loans in Option B. My paperwork check showed shipping cut-offs are a nightmare. We can’t risk another delay!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, Option B’s loans would trigger those transport costs I flagged. Option A’s local pieces avoid that budget bleed entirely.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Toshio, Option A feels safest. Light textiles and local tools respect the floor limit. I’m relieved we can avoid heavy rigging.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Rin, Option C’s visible bench offers presence, but the reconstructions risk exceeding the four-hundred-kilo limit. Option A remains the only safe, dynamic choice.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, but the lab is empty! If the bench is visible, who is actually working there? I need real people, not just a prop!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, I agree. But Option A has no powered displays! No breakdowns, no shipping delays. It’s simple, sturdy, and won’t fail us at the door.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, precisely. No loans, no mounts, no transport. Option A is the only choice that doesn’t hemorrhage cash before the doors even open.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Toshio, I agree. Option A is light and local. It respects the floor limit and avoids the evening event conflicts. It feels safe for the room.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Rin, the craftspeople in Option A are the presence. They are the staff. The data confirms this is what brings people back.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, but the lab is still empty! If the bench is just a prop, I’m stuck! I need to know who actually works there!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, Option A has no bench! It’s just people and cloth. No tech to break, no shipping to miss. It’s the safest bet for us.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, the craftspeople are the staff. No lab, no bench, no hidden costs. Option A is the only budget that actually survives the season.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
